cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use eval_harness in your work, please cite this repository."
title: "eval_harness: a one-click eval suite for code LLMs (Verilog + Triton/CUDA)"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Magicpjl/eval_harness"
abstract: >-
  A single-proxy, two-stage (generate -> stop engine -> shard-verify) evaluation
  harness for code LLMs across Verilog (VerilogEval, RTLLM 2.0, ArchXBench v1.5,
  RealBench-Module, CVDP cid003) and Triton/CUDA (KernelBench L1/L2/L3,
  TritonBench-G) benchmarks. Supports local vLLM or any external
  OpenAI-compatible API endpoint.
authors:
  - name: Magicpjl
    email: Magicpjl@users.noreply.github.com
keywords:
  - llm-evaluation
  - code-generation
  - verilog
  - triton
  - cuda
  - benchmark
  - vllm
